          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For a small warm-season lawn kept short and mowed weekly, a five-blade reel like the Great States 415-16 or the American Lawn Mower 1815-18 gives a finish no rotary can match, for no fuel and almost no noise. If your lawn is tall fescue or bluegrass, the Fiskars StaySharp Max is the only reel here that can mow it at a healthy height.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your lawn is big, bumpy, under trees or likely to go two weeks between mowings, be honest with yourself and buy a rotary. A reel mower rewards the right lawn and the right habits, and it punishes everything else.
          </p>
